QTIP develop lattice, additive, or trellis representations (Tseng et al., 2024a; Egiazarian et al., 2024; Tseng et al., 2024b).
HAWQ-V2 uses sensitivity for mixed precision (Dong et al., 2020), while GSQ and RCO optimize quantization and budget
allocation (Dadgarnia et al., 2026; Helcig and Alistarh, 2026). Pruning removes weights or dimensions; low-rank methods
reduce matrix rank (Frantar and Alistarh, 2023; Sun et al., 2024; Ashkboos et al., 2024a; Wang et al., 2025). Recovery can
use quantization-aware fine-tuning (Malinovskii et al., 2024) or distillation (Hinton et al., 2015; Muralidharan et al., 2024).
Serving systems optimize memory management and attention execution (Kwon et al., 2023; Ye et al., 2025); TinyChat
and QServe couple quantized formats with matching kernels (Lin et al., 2024, 2025).
These methods supply components; we study agents that select, combine, implement, and validate a complete
compressed model.


6 Conclusion
LLM compression provides a concrete task for studying agent-driven model improvement. Across 36 runs, 29 artifacts
pass independent verification. Recorded searches show quality gains at nearly fixed storage, local rankings overturned by


    InfiniAI Lab · Carnegie Mellon University                                                                               11

## Page 12

complete-model feedback, and generation or implementation failures missed by likelihood alone. Effective compression
requires numerical design, experimental judgment, and validation of the final executable model. Extending this step
toward RSI requires testing whether a compressed model retains the ability to carry out subsequent compression tasks.


